Home on the Range is a 2004 American animated Western comedy
film produced by Walt Disney Feature Animation.

12
00:43:25,714 --> 00:43:31,714
Written and directed by Will Finn and John Sanford, it stars the voices of Roseanne Barr,
Judi Dench, Jennifer Tilly, Cuba Gooding Jr., Randy Quaid, and Steve Buscemi.

13
00:47:02,857 --> 00:47:08,857
It features original songs written by Alan Menken and Glenn Slater, and an
original musical orchestral score also composed by Menken.

14
00:50:40,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Home on the Range is set in the Old West, and centers on a mismatched trio
of dairy cows—brash, adventurous Maggie; prim, proper Mrs.

15
00:54:17,142 --> 00:54:23,142
Calloway; and ditzy, happy-go-lucky Grace.

16
00:57:54,285 --> 00:58:00,285
The three cows must capture an infamous rustler named Alameda Slim for his
bounty in order to save their idyllic farm from foreclosure.

17
01:01:31,428 --> 01:01:37,428
Aiding them in their quest is Lucky Jack, a feisty, peg-legged rabbit, and a selfish horse named Buck,
eagerly working in the service of Rico, a famous bounty hunter, who seeks the glory for himself.

18
01:05:08,571 --> 01:05:14,571
Home on the Range premiered at the El Capitan Theatre in Los Angeles on March
21, 2004, and was released in the United States on April 2.

19
